1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,380
What's today's video about? It's all about Japan's unique culture!

2
00:00:09,380 --> 00:00:12,380
Scene 1: How to Enjoy Conveyor Belt Sushi

3
00:00:12,380 --> 00:00:17,114
This is a conveyor belt sushi restaurant.

4
00:00:17,137 --> 00:00:21,794
Wow, there's so much food going around!

5
00:00:21,817 --> 00:00:26,484
Yep, just grab whatever you like and eat.

6
00:00:26,507 --> 00:00:29,782
That's such a fun system!

7
00:00:29,805 --> 00:00:34,772
If you want to order something, use this screen.

8
00:00:34,795 --> 00:00:38,369
Is there an English menu?

9
00:00:38,392 --> 00:00:43,810
Yes, you can change the language on the screen.

10
00:00:43,833 --> 00:00:46,500
That's really convenient!

11
00:00:46,524 --> 00:00:51,491
Tuna is my favorite.

12
00:00:51,514 --> 00:00:56,714
I'm not really a fan of raw fish.

13
00:00:56,737 --> 00:01:01,816
Don't worry, they have sushi with meat or tempura too!

14
00:01:01,840 --> 00:01:04,006
Really?

15
00:01:04,029 --> 00:01:08,678
Yeah, they even have fried shrimp sushi.

16
00:01:08,701 --> 00:01:13,101
In that case, I can eat a lot!

17
00:01:13,124 --> 00:01:16,531
Take a look at the table.

18
00:01:16,555 --> 00:01:19,642
There are so many things here!

19
00:01:19,665 --> 00:01:23,678
This is soy sauce.

20
00:01:23,701 --> 00:01:26,589
What's this green box?

21
00:01:26,613 --> 00:01:30,047
That's wasabi.

22
00:01:30,070 --> 00:01:34,958
Isn't wasabi already inside the sushi?

23
00:01:34,981 --> 00:01:41,181
Nope, none of the sushi here has wasabi in it.

24
00:01:41,204 --> 00:01:44,417
So you add it yourself.

25
00:01:44,440 --> 00:01:49,607
Over there, there's green tea powder, right?

26
00:01:49,630 --> 00:01:52,063
Yes, there is.

27
00:01:52,086 --> 00:01:56,686
Put the powder in the cup.

28
00:01:56,709 --> 00:01:59,288
What do I do after that?

29
00:01:59,312 --> 00:02:04,245
Press the button on the table firmly.

30
00:02:04,268 --> 00:02:07,401
Oh, hot water came out!

31
00:02:07,424 --> 00:02:11,258
Be careful not to burn yourself.

32
00:02:11,281 --> 00:02:15,214
Making it yourself is fun!

33
00:02:15,237 --> 00:02:18,237
Look at the colors of the plates.

34
00:02:18,260 --> 00:02:22,737
There are red and blue plates.

35
00:02:22,761 --> 00:02:26,845
The price changes depending on the color.

36
00:02:26,868 --> 00:02:31,268
How much is this blue plate?

37
00:02:31,291 --> 00:02:34,906
That one is 150 yen.

38
00:02:34,929 --> 00:02:37,529
That's really cheap!

39
00:02:37,552 --> 00:02:42,286
Oh, here comes the sushi we ordered!

40
00:02:42,309 --> 00:02:44,999
Where is it coming from?

41
00:02:45,023 --> 00:02:50,156
It's being delivered by the Shinkansen from the top lane!

42
00:02:50,179 --> 00:02:52,312
That's amazing!

43
00:02:52,335 --> 00:02:57,202
After you take your plate, press the button on the screen.

44
00:02:57,225 --> 00:03:01,363
The Shinkansen is heading back.

45
00:03:01,386 --> 00:03:05,353
Alright, let's eat while it's still warm!

46
00:03:05,376 --> 00:03:07,455
Let's dig in!

47
00:03:07,479 --> 00:03:09,846
Does it taste good?

48
00:03:09,869 --> 00:03:13,202
Yes, it's delicious!

49
00:03:13,225 --> 00:03:17,891
After you finish eating, stack the plates on the table.

50
00:03:17,914 --> 00:03:21,881
Should I stack plates of the same color together?

51
00:03:21,904 --> 00:03:28,748
Yes, stacking plates of the same color makes it easier to tally up later.

52
00:03:28,771 --> 00:03:30,816
Got it.

53
00:03:30,840 --> 00:03:36,055
At this place, you can even drop the plates into slots.

54
00:03:36,079 --> 00:03:39,055
Slots for the plates?

55
00:03:39,078 --> 00:03:44,770
That’s right—drop in five plates, and the game starts.

56
00:03:44,794 --> 00:03:48,727
If we win the game, do we get something?

57
00:03:48,750 --> 00:03:52,837
You’ll get a small toy!

58
00:03:52,861 --> 00:03:57,061
That sounds fun—let’s eat a lot!

59
00:03:57,084 --> 00:04:04,189
You can review today’s video with the link in the description and top comment. *Note: The site may be removed without notice.

60
00:04:04,189 --> 00:04:07,189
Scene 2: The Charm of Food Samples

61
00:04:07,189 --> 00:04:12,072
Next, let’s head to a food sample shop.

62
00:04:12,095 --> 00:04:14,270
Food samples?

63
00:04:14,293 --> 00:04:20,293
Yes—the fake food displays you see at restaurant entrances.

64
00:04:20,316 --> 00:04:24,160
Oh, I’ve seen those on TV!

65
00:04:24,183 --> 00:04:28,820
This shop has all kinds of samples.

66
00:04:28,844 --> 00:04:33,977
Wow, this spaghetti looks so real!

67
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:37,615
The fork’s just floating in midair!

68
00:04:37,639 --> 00:04:40,447
Why doesn’t it fall?

69
00:04:40,470 --> 00:04:45,716
Because the samples are made of hard plastic.

70
00:04:45,740 --> 00:04:48,155
That’s amazing craftsmanship!

71
00:04:48,179 --> 00:04:52,217
Over there, they even have sushi samples.

72
00:04:52,241 --> 00:04:56,644
The tuna’s oil texture looks so lifelike.

73
00:04:56,667 --> 00:05:01,003
You can touch them, but please don’t break anything.

74
00:05:01,026 --> 00:05:04,560
Does it feel a little soft if you press it?

75
00:05:04,583 --> 00:05:09,655
No, it’s plastic—it’s hard.

76
00:05:09,678 --> 00:05:13,278
You’d never tell just by looking.

77
00:05:13,301 --> 00:05:19,117
They used to be made of wax, but the materials have changed.

78
00:05:19,141 --> 00:05:21,941
So they don’t age or wear out.

79
00:05:21,964 --> 00:05:26,254
Exactly—they won’t melt, even on hot summer days.

80
00:05:26,278 --> 00:05:30,045
Other countries don’t have samples like this.

81
00:05:30,068 --> 00:05:35,886
In Japan, you can see what the dishes look like before even checking the menu.

82
00:05:35,910 --> 00:05:40,581
It’s super helpful for tourists who can’t read kanji.

83
00:05:40,604 --> 00:05:45,371
This shop even lets you try making samples yourself.

84
00:05:45,394 --> 00:05:48,727
We can make them ourselves?

85
00:05:48,750 --> 00:05:53,848
Yes—you can craft tempura or lettuce samples.

86
00:05:53,871 --> 00:05:57,769
That sounds fun—I want to try!

87
00:05:57,793 --> 00:06:02,326
You can also buy mini keychains as souvenirs.

88
00:06:02,349 --> 00:06:05,838
There’s a ramen keychain!

89
00:06:05,861 --> 00:06:10,733
I’ll take this tiny beer bottle keychain.

90
00:06:10,757 --> 00:06:15,123
The foam details are just like the real thing!

91
00:06:15,146 --> 00:06:18,980
Your friends will love it if you give it to them.

92
00:06:19,003 --> 00:06:22,203
Oh, they’ll definitely be surprised!

93
00:06:22,226 --> 00:06:26,668
Alright, let’s book a sample-making session.

94
00:06:26,691 --> 00:06:28,729
Thank you!

95
00:06:28,752 --> 00:06:37,691
If you caught what we said, leave a comment!

96
00:06:37,691 --> 00:06:40,691
Scene 3: How to Enjoy Animal Cafés

97
00:06:40,691 --> 00:06:44,861
Next, let’s visit an animal café.

98
00:06:44,885 --> 00:06:46,924
An animal café?

99
00:06:46,947 --> 00:06:53,221
Yes—a place where you can sip tea while surrounded by adorable animals.

100
00:06:53,244 --> 00:06:57,729
Japan has so many different kinds of animal cafés!

101
00:06:57,753 --> 00:07:02,753
Yes, cat cafés and dog cafés are quite famous.

102
00:07:02,776 --> 00:07:07,109
I saw a café for miniature Shiba Inus on TV.

103
00:07:07,132 --> 00:07:11,966
They’re so tiny and incredibly cute!

104
00:07:11,989 --> 00:07:15,679
Are there cafés for owls or hedgehogs too?

105
00:07:15,703 --> 00:07:20,371
Oh yes, they’ve become really popular lately.

106
00:07:20,395 --> 00:07:25,204
I love birds, so I’d love to visit an owl café.

107
00:07:25,227 --> 00:07:29,505
Then let’s head to the owl café nearby!

108
00:07:29,528 --> 00:07:34,129
Are there any rules we should know before entering?

109
00:07:34,153 --> 00:07:38,920
Yes, please wash your hands first.

110
00:07:38,943 --> 00:07:42,042
Do we also need to disinfect with alcohol?

111
00:07:42,065 --> 00:07:47,065
Yes, it’s necessary to prevent diseases in the animals.

112
00:07:47,088 --> 00:07:48,695
Got it.

113
00:07:48,718 --> 00:07:53,518
Also, avoid speaking loudly.

114
00:07:53,541 --> 00:07:56,908
The animals might get startled.

115
00:07:56,931 --> 00:07:59,531
Can we take photos?

116
00:07:59,554 --> 00:08:04,087
Photos are fine, but don’t use the flash.

117
00:08:04,110 --> 00:08:08,477
Bright light can harm the birds’ eyes.

118
00:08:08,500 --> 00:08:11,067
Got it, we’ll be careful.

119
00:08:11,090 --> 00:08:15,023
Look, there’s a big owl over there!

120
00:08:15,046 --> 00:08:18,728
Wow, it’s so calm and adorable.

121
00:08:18,752 --> 00:08:21,233
Can I touch it?

122
00:08:21,256 --> 00:08:25,509
You can pet the owls with the yellow stickers.

123
00:08:25,533 --> 00:08:29,866
Gently stroke the back of its head.

124
00:08:29,889 --> 00:08:32,742
It feels so soft!

125
00:08:32,765 --> 00:08:36,015
The owl is closing its eyes.

126
00:08:36,038 --> 00:08:39,238
They close their eyes when they’re comfortable.

127
00:08:39,261 --> 00:08:44,061
That owl over there has a different sticker color.

128
00:08:44,084 --> 00:08:47,418
Don’t touch the owls with red stickers.

129
00:08:47,441 --> 00:08:50,923
It’s a little grumpy right now.

130
00:08:50,946 --> 00:08:55,146
Be careful—it might bite.

131
00:08:55,169 --> 00:08:59,409
Where do we order food and drinks?

132
00:08:59,432 --> 00:09:03,507
Buy a ticket from the vending machine at the entrance.

133
00:09:03,531 --> 00:09:06,098
It’s a cup with a lid, right?

134
00:09:06,121 --> 00:09:10,087
Yes, we use lids to keep bird feathers out.

135
00:09:10,110 --> 00:09:12,719
That’s very thoughtful.

136
00:09:12,743 --> 00:09:15,476
There’s a time limit here.

137
00:09:15,499 --> 00:09:17,943
How much is it per hour?

138
00:09:17,966 --> 00:09:20,900
It’s 1,500 yen per person.

139
00:09:20,923 --> 00:09:23,889
That includes a drink.

140
00:09:23,912 --> 00:09:26,346
I think that’s a great deal!

141
00:09:26,369 --> 00:09:31,135
This was so relaxing. Let’s tackle work again tomorrow with fresh energy!

142
00:09:31,158 --> 00:09:34,192
Absolutely, let’s come back again!

143
00:09:34,215 --> 00:09:37,215
Scene 4: How to Use Vending Machines in Japan

144
00:09:37,215 --> 00:09:42,626
Wow, there are so many vending machines!

145
00:09:42,649 --> 00:09:47,660
Yeah, they’re everywhere in Japan.

146
00:09:47,683 --> 00:09:53,360
We don’t have many in my country, so this is really unusual.

147
00:09:53,383 --> 00:09:58,616
I’m thirsty—shall we grab a drink?

148
00:09:58,639 --> 00:10:00,373
Sure!

149
00:10:00,396 --> 00:10:01,833
Let’s do it.

150
00:10:01,856 --> 00:10:04,503
What would you like to drink?

151
00:10:04,526 --> 00:10:08,464
I’d love an iced tea.

152
00:10:08,487 --> 00:10:11,498
Take a look below the buttons.

153
00:10:11,522 --> 00:10:16,822
Oh, there are blue and red colors, aren't there?

154
00:10:16,845 --> 00:10:20,478
The blue ones are for cold drinks.

155
00:10:20,501 --> 00:10:23,789
So, what are the red ones for?

156
00:10:23,813 --> 00:10:27,618
The red ones are for hot drinks.

157
00:10:27,641 --> 00:10:31,641
Are there hot drinks even in the summer?

158
00:10:31,664 --> 00:10:36,721
Yes, coffee and tea are available all year round.

159
00:10:36,745 --> 00:10:39,522
That's amazing!

160
00:10:39,545 --> 00:10:44,413
In winter, you can also buy hot soup.

161
00:10:44,436 --> 00:10:48,603
Are there vending machines for soup too?

162
00:10:48,626 --> 00:10:53,430
Yes, there’s corn soup and miso soup.

163
00:10:53,454 --> 00:10:56,287
They come in cans, right?

164
00:10:56,310 --> 00:11:01,843
Yes, they’re very warming, so they’re popular in winter.

165
00:11:01,866 --> 00:11:04,866
I’d love to try them in winter.

166
00:11:04,889 --> 00:11:07,456
Which button is for tea?

167
00:11:07,479 --> 00:11:11,012
This green can button, right here.

168
00:11:11,035 --> 00:11:15,235
Yes, it’s 160 yen.

169
00:11:15,258 --> 00:11:18,066
Where do I put the money?

170
00:11:18,089 --> 00:11:22,302
Here’s the slot for bills.

171
00:11:22,326 --> 00:11:25,621
The coin slot is on the right, isn’t it?

172
00:11:25,644 --> 00:11:28,010
Yes, that’s right.

173
00:11:28,033 --> 00:11:31,967
Can I pay with my smartphone these days?

174
00:11:31,990 --> 00:11:36,790
Yes, you can easily buy with an app.

175
00:11:36,813 --> 00:11:40,146
So I don’t even need cash!

176
00:11:40,169 --> 00:11:44,624
Now insert the money and press the button.

177
00:11:44,648 --> 00:11:47,126
Okay, I pressed it.

178
00:11:47,149 --> 00:11:51,482
The drink came out from the bottom, didn’t it?

179
00:11:51,505 --> 00:11:54,339
It made a loud *clunk* sound!

180
00:11:54,362 --> 00:11:57,768
Don’t forget to take your change.

181
00:11:57,791 --> 00:12:00,591
Oh, that was close!

182
00:12:00,614 --> 00:12:05,032
There’s a square box next to the vending machine, isn’t there?

183
00:12:05,055 --> 00:12:07,022
Yes, there is.

184
00:12:07,045 --> 00:12:11,982
That’s a recycling bin for empty cans and PET bottles.

185
00:12:12,006 --> 00:12:15,412
I’ll put mine there when I’m done.

186
00:12:15,435 --> 00:12:19,235
Yes, don’t litter on the street.

187
00:12:19,258 --> 00:12:21,073
Got it.

188
00:12:21,097 --> 00:12:23,430
I’ll follow the rules.

189
00:12:23,453 --> 00:12:26,453
Scene 5: How to Enjoy Karaoke

190
00:12:26,453 --> 00:12:30,686
We’re at a karaoke box today.

191
00:12:30,709 --> 00:12:34,509
Wow, there are so many rooms!

192
00:12:34,532 --> 00:12:39,766
Yes, this is where you sing.

193
00:12:39,789 --> 00:12:45,922
This is my first time at a Japanese karaoke, so I’m really excited!

194
00:12:45,945 --> 00:12:52,217
We got our room number at the front desk, so let’s go in.

195
00:12:52,240 --> 00:12:57,007
There’s a big screen in this room!

196
00:12:57,030 --> 00:13:01,929
Yes, the song lyrics will appear on that screen.

197
00:13:01,953 --> 00:13:06,720
What’s that small machine on the table?

198
00:13:06,743 --> 00:13:12,676
That’s called a *denmoku*—it’s for selecting songs.

199
00:13:12,699 --> 00:13:16,099
Are there English or Vietnamese songs too?

200
00:13:16,122 --> 00:13:21,988
Yes, you can change the language on the screen.

201
00:13:22,011 --> 00:13:27,045
Then I can sing songs from my country too!

202
00:13:27,068 --> 00:13:32,270
Choose the song you want and press the send button.

203
00:13:32,293 --> 00:13:36,026
Oh, the song title appeared on the screen!

204
00:13:36,049 --> 00:13:41,449
Grab the mic, stand over there, and sing your heart out!

205
00:13:41,472 --> 00:13:45,639
I’m a little embarrassed, but I’ll do my best to sing!

206
00:13:45,662 --> 00:13:50,875
If the volume’s too loud, just turn it down with this button.

207
00:13:50,899 --> 00:13:52,866
Got it.

208
00:13:52,889 --> 00:13:56,692
Can we dim the lights in the room too?

209
00:13:56,715 --> 00:14:01,812
Yes, you can adjust the brightness with the switch on the wall.

210
00:14:01,835 --> 00:14:04,669
This is such a great atmosphere!

211
00:14:04,692 --> 00:14:09,092
Oh, there’s a menu on the table.

212
00:14:09,115 --> 00:14:13,481
There’s so much food and drinks!

213
00:14:13,504 --> 00:14:16,802
The fried potatoes and pizza are really popular.

214
00:14:16,826 --> 00:14:19,678
How do I order something?

215
00:14:19,701 --> 00:14:23,678
Just use the black phone on the wall.

216
00:14:23,702 --> 00:14:27,269
Will the staff bring it to our room?

217
00:14:27,292 --> 00:14:32,692
Yeah, they’ll open the door and bring it right in.

218
00:14:32,715 --> 00:14:35,563
This system is so convenient!

219
00:14:35,586 --> 00:14:41,924
In Japan, there’s even a culture called 'Hitora' where people come alone.

220
00:14:41,947 --> 00:14:45,080
You come to karaoke by yourself?

221
00:14:45,103 --> 00:14:51,336
Yeah, it’s a great way to practice without worrying about others.

222
00:14:51,359 --> 00:14:54,334
It sounds perfect for when you’re stressed.

223
00:14:54,358 --> 00:14:59,358
Yeah, singing at the top of your lungs is so refreshing!

224
00:14:59,381 --> 00:15:02,914
I think I’ll try coming alone next time.

225
00:15:02,937 --> 00:15:06,414
Our time is almost up.

226
00:15:06,438 --> 00:15:10,378
Is there any signal before the time runs out?

227
00:15:10,401 --> 00:15:15,887
Yes, the room phone will ring ten minutes before the end.

228
00:15:15,910 --> 00:15:20,315
Will they say, 'You have ten minutes left' over the phone?

229
00:15:20,338 --> 00:15:24,576
Yeah, so you’ll know how much time is left.

230
00:15:24,599 --> 00:15:27,799
Let’s sing one last song together!

231
00:15:27,822 --> 00:15:29,507
Sure!

232
00:15:29,531 --> 00:15:32,498
How about an anime song?

233
00:15:32,521 --> 00:15:37,170
After we finish singing, we’ll pay together at the front desk.

234
00:15:37,193 --> 00:15:40,193
Scene 6: Introduction to Pachinko

235
00:15:40,193 --> 00:15:43,827
This is a pachinko parlor, right?

236
00:15:43,850 --> 00:15:50,016
Yeah, it’s like a huge arcade unique to Japan.

237
00:15:50,039 --> 00:15:54,618
You can hear the loud noises even from outside.

238
00:15:54,641 --> 00:15:58,008
It’s even louder inside!

239
00:15:58,031 --> 00:16:03,564
When the door opened, I saw so many flashing lights!

240
00:16:03,587 --> 00:16:07,954
Yeah, there are rows and rows of machines.

241
00:16:07,977 --> 00:16:12,710
Can foreigners like me play too?

242
00:16:12,733 --> 00:16:18,710
Yes, as long as you’re 18 or older, anyone can play!

243
00:16:18,734 --> 00:16:20,216
Great!

244
00:16:20,239 --> 00:16:22,715
How do you play?

245
00:16:22,739 --> 00:16:26,626
First, sit at an open seat.

246
00:16:26,650 --> 00:16:30,883
Then you put money into the machine?

247
00:16:30,906 --> 00:16:32,401
Yes.

248
00:16:32,425 --> 00:16:36,492
Inserting bills will charge the machine with credits.

249
00:16:36,515 --> 00:16:39,004
What’s next?

250
00:16:39,027 --> 00:16:42,295
Press the button to get your pachinko balls.

251
00:16:42,319 --> 00:16:46,852
Oh, a bunch of little silver balls came out!

252
00:16:46,875 --> 00:16:49,853
You use those balls to play.

253
00:16:49,877 --> 00:16:54,244
What’s the round handle on the bottom right for?

254
00:16:54,267 --> 00:16:59,134
Turning it to the right shoots the balls upward.

255
00:16:59,156 --> 00:17:04,026
The strength you turn it changes where the balls go, right?

256
00:17:04,050 --> 00:17:08,061
Alright, try to aim for the best spots!

257
00:17:08,084 --> 00:17:11,018
Look, the numbers on the screen are moving!

258
00:17:11,041 --> 00:17:15,807
If the ball goes into the center hole, the screen will react!

259
00:17:15,830 --> 00:17:19,964
What happens if three of the same numbers line up?

260
00:17:19,987 --> 00:17:24,086
That’s a jackpot! You’ll get tons of balls!

261
00:17:24,110 --> 00:17:28,310
Wow, that sounds so exciting!

262
00:17:28,333 --> 00:17:32,533
But don’t spend too much money, okay?

263
00:17:32,556 --> 00:17:36,135
Got it! I’ll set a time limit for playing.

264
00:17:36,158 --> 00:17:39,806
When you’re done, press the return button.

265
00:17:39,830 --> 00:17:42,696
Here’s your leftover balance card.

266
00:17:42,719 --> 00:17:48,207
Just insert that card into the cashier machine, and you’ll get your money back.

267
00:17:48,231 --> 00:17:51,068
What should I do with the balls I won?

268
00:17:51,091 --> 00:17:55,458
You can put them in a box or count them using the machine.

269
00:17:55,481 --> 00:17:59,014
Can I exchange them for prizes afterward?

270
00:17:59,037 --> 00:18:04,637
Yes! At the prize counter, you can trade them for snacks, pens, and more.

271
00:18:04,660 --> 00:18:07,867
That’ll make a unique souvenir!

272
00:18:07,891 --> 00:18:11,524
You got to experience a special part of Japanese culture!

273
00:18:11,547 --> 00:18:15,219
Yeah, it was such a fun experience!

274
00:18:15,243 --> 00:18:18,243
Scene 7: How to Use a Manga Café

275
00:18:18,243 --> 00:18:21,724
This is a manga café, right?

276
00:18:21,747 --> 00:18:26,014
Yes, it’s also called an internet café.

277
00:18:26,037 --> 00:18:29,603
There are so many books here!

278
00:18:29,626 --> 00:18:35,026
Yep! You can read any manga here.

279
00:18:35,049 --> 00:18:40,816
I love Japanese manga, so this is amazing!

280
00:18:40,839 --> 00:18:44,246
Did you get a card at the reception?

281
00:18:44,269 --> 00:18:47,403
Yes, I got this card.

282
00:18:47,426 --> 00:18:50,900
Your room number is written on it.

283
00:18:50,924 --> 00:18:53,490
It’s room number three.

284
00:18:53,513 --> 00:18:56,913
Let’s go together!

285
00:18:56,936 --> 00:19:01,831
Oh, this is a small private booth!

286
00:19:01,855 --> 00:19:05,488
Yes, and you can even lock the door.

287
00:19:05,511 --> 00:19:09,357
There’s a computer and a big chair too!

288
00:19:09,381 --> 00:19:14,614
This chair turns into a bed, so you can even sleep here!

289
00:19:14,637 --> 00:19:17,848
Do people stay overnight here?

290
00:19:17,872 --> 00:19:22,321
Yes, many people use it as an alternative to hotels.

291
00:19:22,345 --> 00:19:25,025
How much does it cost?

292
00:19:25,049 --> 00:19:28,922
Around 1,500 yen for three hours.

293
00:19:28,945 --> 00:19:32,578
That’s way cheaper than a hotel!

294
00:19:32,601 --> 00:19:37,269
I’m thirsty—let’s grab a drink!

295
00:19:37,293 --> 00:19:39,929
Where can we get drinks?

296
00:19:39,953 --> 00:19:44,793
All the drinks over there are free!

297
00:19:44,816 --> 00:19:48,550
Wait, we don’t have to pay?

298
00:19:48,573 --> 00:19:52,856
Nope! Juice, coffee—everything’s all-you-can-drink.

299
00:19:52,879 --> 00:19:55,713
What a great system!

300
00:19:55,736 --> 00:19:59,613
There’s even ice cream—help yourself!

301
00:19:59,636 --> 00:20:02,916
Can I eat it while reading manga?

302
00:20:02,940 --> 00:20:07,307
Sure! You can bring it to your room.

303
00:20:07,330 --> 00:20:10,167
Are there shower rooms too?

304
00:20:10,191 --> 00:20:14,457
Yes, you can use them for a small fee at the reception.

305
00:20:14,480 --> 00:20:17,514
Do they provide towels and toothbrushes too?

306
00:20:17,537 --> 00:20:21,029
Yes, you can buy it at the store.

307
00:20:21,052 --> 00:20:24,121
They really have everything here, don't they?

308
00:20:24,145 --> 00:20:27,578
Please keep it down inside the room.

309
00:20:27,601 --> 00:20:31,201
I’ll watch something on my computer using headphones.

310
00:20:31,224 --> 00:20:34,697
Right, we shouldn’t make loud noises.

311
00:20:34,720 --> 00:20:38,328
We don’t want to disturb the people in the next room.

312
00:20:38,352 --> 00:20:42,289
Alright, let’s dive into some manga!

313
00:20:42,313 --> 00:20:45,392
I’ll be here until night.

314
00:20:45,415 --> 00:20:48,415
Scene 8: The Joy of Solo Yakiniku / How to Savor Yakiniku Alone

315
00:20:48,415 --> 00:20:52,884
This is a yakiniku restaurant specializing in solo dining, isn’t it?

316
00:20:52,907 --> 00:20:59,123
Yes, it’s a place where you can quietly enjoy yakiniku all by yourself.

317
00:20:59,147 --> 00:21:03,880
There’s a vending machine at the entrance, I see.

318
00:21:03,903 --> 00:21:08,319
Right, you buy your ticket here first.

319
00:21:08,342 --> 00:21:12,942
I got a ticket for the karubi set.

320
00:21:12,966 --> 00:21:17,499
Now, let’s go inside and take a seat.

321
00:21:17,522 --> 00:21:22,979
Oh, the seats are partitioned one by one.

322
00:21:23,003 --> 00:21:30,570
Yes, you can’t see the person next to you, so you can eat at your own pace.

323
00:21:30,593 --> 00:21:34,326
There’s a small grill on the table.

324
00:21:34,349 --> 00:21:38,404
That’s a personal yakiniku grill.

325
00:21:38,428 --> 00:21:42,028
Can I light the grill myself?

326
00:21:42,051 --> 00:21:47,051
Yes, just press the button in front of you to light it.

327
00:21:47,074 --> 00:21:50,944
There’s a touchscreen right in front of me.

328
00:21:50,967 --> 00:21:57,101
Yes, you can order more meat or adjust your rice portion there.

329
00:21:57,124 --> 00:22:02,257
I’d like to get a large serving of rice.

330
00:22:02,280 --> 00:22:06,748
Just press the rice button on the screen.

331
00:22:06,772 --> 00:22:11,705
Are there a lot of people in Japan who eat yakiniku alone?

332
00:22:11,728 --> 00:22:15,134
Yes, there are quite a few.

333
00:22:15,157 --> 00:22:21,030
In my country, yakiniku is always eaten with family or friends.

334
00:22:21,054 --> 00:22:25,721
In Japan, we have a term called 'ohitorisama.'

335
00:22:25,744 --> 00:22:28,425
What does 'ohitorisama' mean?

336
00:22:28,448 --> 00:22:34,136
It refers to people who enjoy dining out or traveling alone.

337
00:22:34,160 --> 00:22:37,361
Isn’t it lonely to eat alone?

338
00:22:37,385 --> 00:22:44,658
Not at all—you can eat what you want, when you want. It’s liberating!

339
00:22:44,681 --> 00:22:50,081
These days, it’s normal to go to ramen shops or karaoke alone too.

340
00:22:50,104 --> 00:22:56,471
Yes, in Japan, doing things solo is just part of the culture.

341
00:22:56,493 --> 00:23:00,660
So you don’t have to worry about what others think?

342
00:23:00,683 --> 00:23:06,816
Oh, the meat set just came up from under the counter!

343
00:23:06,839 --> 00:23:09,906
That meat looks delicious!

344
00:23:09,929 --> 00:23:13,562
The sauce dish is included too.

345
00:23:13,586 --> 00:23:16,819
Where’s the sauce?

346
00:23:16,842 --> 00:23:21,677
There are bottles of different sauces lined up in front of your seat.

347
00:23:21,700 --> 00:23:26,034
I see soy sauce and lemon juice.

348
00:23:26,057 --> 00:23:31,063
Yes, feel free to use whichever sauce you like.

349
00:23:31,086 --> 00:23:34,331
Alright, let’s grill some meat!

350
00:23:34,354 --> 00:23:39,488
Use the tongs to place it on the grill.

351
00:23:39,511 --> 00:23:43,077
It’s making that nice sizzling sound!

352
00:23:43,100 --> 00:23:46,834
Don’t overcook it.

353
00:23:46,857 --> 00:23:49,657
Got it, I’ll flip it.

354
00:23:49,680 --> 00:23:54,317
Grilling meat just for yourself feels like such a luxury.

355
00:23:54,340 --> 00:23:59,590
Absolutely—no one’s going to take your meat. It’s the best!

356
00:23:59,614 --> 00:24:03,380
Please enjoy the meat with your rice.

357
00:24:03,403 --> 00:24:08,003
The sauce is rich and goes perfectly with rice.

358
00:24:08,026 --> 00:24:14,267
If the grill gets dirty, you can request a replacement using the touch panel.

359
00:24:14,291 --> 00:24:18,185
You can do everything without even calling the staff.

360
00:24:18,209 --> 00:24:23,076
Yes, you can fully enjoy your own personal time.

361
00:24:23,099 --> 00:24:26,335
I’m completely full today.

362
00:24:26,358 --> 00:24:31,158
After eating, take your receipt to the register to pay.

363
00:24:31,182 --> 00:24:33,553
That was delicious. Thank you for the meal!

364
00:24:33,576 --> 00:24:36,576
Scene 9: How to Use a Capsule Hotel

365
00:24:36,576 --> 00:24:41,377
We’re staying at a capsule hotel tonight.

366
00:24:41,401 --> 00:24:47,401
Yes, this is a uniquely Japanese and fascinating type of hotel.

367
00:24:47,423 --> 00:24:51,037
Do we take off our shoes at the entrance?

368
00:24:51,061 --> 00:24:55,752
Yes, please remove your shoes and put them in the locker.

369
00:24:55,775 --> 00:24:57,813
Got it.

370
00:24:57,837 --> 00:25:00,046
I’ve locked the locker.

371
00:25:00,069 --> 00:25:04,236
Now, take the key and head to the reception desk.

372
00:25:04,259 --> 00:25:08,192
We’ll check in here.

373
00:25:08,215 --> 00:25:12,582
Yes, pay the fee and receive your key.

374
00:25:12,605 --> 00:25:18,102
My key is for capsule number 201.

375
00:25:18,125 --> 00:25:22,258
I got the key for capsule 301.

376
00:25:22,281 --> 00:25:26,252
Why are our floors different?

377
00:25:26,276 --> 00:25:33,943
Because capsule hotels have completely separate areas for men and women.

378
00:25:33,966 --> 00:25:38,776
Wait, we can’t go to the same floor?

379
00:25:38,799 --> 00:25:42,775
No, the elevators are separate too.

380
00:25:42,798 --> 00:25:47,265
We can’t enter floors for the opposite gender.

381
00:25:47,288 --> 00:25:53,121
Right, the elevator won’t move without a keycard.

382
00:25:53,145 --> 00:25:57,583
That’s a safe and great system.

383
00:25:57,606 --> 00:26:03,606
Yes, so women can stay here with peace of mind.

384
00:26:03,629 --> 00:26:10,799
Even so, in this video’s setting, we’re traveling together.

385
00:26:10,823 --> 00:26:12,956
Ah, that’s true.

386
00:26:12,979 --> 00:26:16,861
This is a meta-commentary from the script.

387
00:26:16,884 --> 00:26:21,531
In a real hotel, this is where we’d say goodbye.

388
00:26:21,554 --> 00:26:27,088
Yes, from here, we’ll go our separate ways inside.

389
00:26:27,111 --> 00:26:30,119
Is it quiet inside the capsules?

390
00:26:30,142 --> 00:26:34,109
Yes, everyone sleeps quietly.

391
00:26:34,131 --> 00:26:37,739
We shouldn’t talk loudly.

392
00:26:37,763 --> 00:26:43,258
No loud alarms or phone sounds either.

393
00:26:43,281 --> 00:26:46,571
Always use earphones.

394
00:26:46,595 --> 00:26:49,828
Where do we put our luggage?

395
00:26:49,851 --> 00:26:54,418
There are large lockers where you can store them.

396
00:26:54,441 --> 00:26:58,642
Towels and clothes are also provided in the locker.

397
00:26:58,665 --> 00:27:01,870
Is there a lock inside the capsule?

398
00:27:01,894 --> 00:27:07,033
No, the capsule entrance only has a blind.

399
00:27:07,057 --> 00:27:10,347
We can’t lock it.

400
00:27:10,371 --> 00:27:16,258
Right, so keep valuables in the small safe.

401
00:27:16,281 --> 00:27:19,721
Got it, I’ll be careful.

402
00:27:19,745 --> 00:27:23,711
There’s a spacious public bath available.

403
00:27:23,734 --> 00:27:28,136
You can relax and unwind from your travels there.

404
00:27:28,160 --> 00:27:33,726
Yes, the sauna feels amazing too.

405
00:27:33,749 --> 00:27:38,321
Let’s meet again in the lobby tomorrow morning.

406
00:27:38,345 --> 00:27:41,945
Yes, rest well tonight.

407
00:27:41,968 --> 00:27:44,041
Good night.

408
00:27:44,065 --> 00:27:47,065
Scene 10: A Fun and Unique Experience at a Maid Café

409
00:27:47,065 --> 00:27:48,270
V.

410
00:27:48,294 --> 00:27:51,894
This is a maid café, right?

411
00:27:51,916 --> 00:27:57,050
Yes, it's a very pop and uniquely Japanese café.

412
00:27:57,073 --> 00:28:01,350
Look, the maids are waving at us at the entrance!

413
00:28:01,373 --> 00:28:06,657
Once we go inside, there’s a fun greeting waiting for us.

414
00:28:06,681 --> 00:28:09,081
What kind of greeting?

415
00:28:09,104 --> 00:28:14,981
They say, 'Welcome home, milady, master!'

416
00:28:15,004 --> 00:28:18,771
Wow, they really said it!

417
00:28:18,794 --> 00:28:23,327
It’s a little embarrassing, but so much fun.

418
00:28:23,350 --> 00:28:26,384
Yeah, it’s a really fun experience.

419
00:28:26,407 --> 00:28:30,140
First, let’s hear about the café’s rules.

420
00:28:30,163 --> 00:28:34,763
We can’t just take photos of the maids without permission.

421
00:28:34,786 --> 00:28:39,359
Right, there’s a camera symbol with an X on it.

422
00:28:39,382 --> 00:28:43,121
And touching the maids is also not allowed.

423
00:28:43,145 --> 00:28:47,378
Yes, so make sure to follow the rules.

424
00:28:47,401 --> 00:28:51,134
Oh, the maid is bringing the menu now.

425
00:28:51,157 --> 00:28:54,924
Curry and omurice are really popular here.

426
00:28:54,947 --> 00:28:58,280
I’ll go with the omurice.

427
00:28:58,303 --> 00:29:02,784
The maid will draw a picture on it with ketchup for you.

428
00:29:02,807 --> 00:29:05,077
What kind of picture should we get?

429
00:29:05,101 --> 00:29:09,034
Let’s ask for a cute cat drawing.

430
00:29:09,057 --> 00:29:12,824
Excuse me, could you draw a cat for us, please?

431
00:29:12,847 --> 00:29:17,502
Wow, the maid is really good at drawing!

432
00:29:17,525 --> 00:29:21,981
Did they ask if we want to do something before eating?

433
00:29:22,004 --> 00:29:27,449
Yes, we’ll say a magic spell together to make it taste even better.

434
00:29:27,473 --> 00:29:30,546
A magic spell?

435
00:29:30,569 --> 00:29:36,302
We say, 'Make it delicious! Moe moe kyun!'

436
00:29:36,325 --> 00:29:39,525
Should we do a pose with the maid too?

437
00:29:39,549 --> 00:29:44,549
Yes, make a heart shape with your hands.

438
00:29:44,572 --> 00:29:48,105
It’s a little embarrassing, but I’ll try it.

439
00:29:48,128 --> 00:29:51,561
Now that we’ve done that, let’s eat!

440
00:29:51,584 --> 00:29:53,918
How does it taste?

441
00:29:53,941 --> 00:29:59,397
It’s just regular omurice, but it feels extra special.

442
00:29:59,420 --> 00:30:02,511
What’s that stage over there for?

443
00:30:02,534 --> 00:30:08,539
When the time comes, the maids perform songs and dances.

444
00:30:08,563 --> 00:30:11,445
So we can watch a live performance?

445
00:30:11,469 --> 00:30:17,248
Yes, and if you buy a ticket, you can even take a cheki photo with them.

446
00:30:17,271 --> 00:30:20,279
Cheki is a small instant photo, right?

447
00:30:20,303 --> 00:30:23,980
Yes, it makes a great keepsake.

448
00:30:24,004 --> 00:30:28,237
Japanese otaku culture is really something else.

449
00:30:28,260 --> 00:30:33,693
It’s super popular with foreigners too, so I’m glad we came today.

450
00:30:33,716 --> 00:30:37,718
Yeah, this was a wonderful experience.